..............",".........................................................",".........................................................",".........................................................","..........................................gggggg.........","..........................................gggggg.........","..........................................gggggg.........",".........................................................",".........................................................","........................................................."],"visible":true,"locked":false,"hiddenForeground":false}],"entities":[],"notes":[],"lootRules":[],"lootPools":{},"itemsByCell":{"fg:763":{"mode":"single","entries":[{"value":"makeshiftheadlamp","percent":100}],"maxDrops":1,"rollIndependent":true},"fg:870":{"mode":"single","entries":[{"value":"emissivecrystalshard","percent":100}],"maxDrops":1,"rollIndependent":true},"fg:764":{"mode":"single","entries":[{"value":"syringe","percent":100}],"maxDrops":1,"rollIndependent":true}},"objectsByCell":{"fg:872":{"id":"trader1"},"fg:713":{"id":"geotree"},"fg:647":{"id":"lorenote"},"fg:1868":{"id":"corpse"}},"customPropertiesByCell":{"647":{"object":{"text":"I met...a walking corpse. \n\nI found them near my new home. Their left arm was just gone, rotting away, they could barely stand straight, and they had a fever that was high enough to completely render my icepack useless in 2 minutes.\n\nThey looked white like the milkys I see usually but... They had the same head shape as my species. And their brighter, yellower eyes... But somehow making eye contact felt safer than with anyone else i've met.\nAfter talking about their life for a good while, they just... handed me everything. They had no chip as i found out upon our discussions, and that they were dropped for being too \"pathetic\" ...as one of the humans put it. They didn't seem upset, though. They actually smiled. The whole time we spent conversating, They seemed content with it all and even ate a geofruit I grabbed from the tree here. I was able to use the last of my aed battery to assess vitals. \nThey were already having an arrythmia. They said they had their arm stuck for a while before they could get it free from the blade... They lost too much blood to fight off whatever instantly gave it necrosis.\n\nI had a near full syringe of heroin. They had instant sleeping pills in their purse.\n \nThey didn't hesitate to ask.\n\nIt was better that they never suffered a worse fate. \n\nI let them listen to my mp3 player before I injected everything and let them lay in a soft bed I made for them with some quick foliage pieces i found around the place.\n\nAll they said was \"Thank you.\"\n\nI hope they rest happy, and well. Somehow, I felt comforted knowing they found me here.","font":"experiment"}},"763":{"item":{"conditionPercent":"0"}},"870":{"item":{"conditionPercent":"0"}},"1868":{"object":{"Visual":"corpse7"}}},"terrainGenAreas":[],"editor":{"activeTool":"select","brushSize":1,"brushShape":"square","selectShape":"box","shapeMode":"filled","shapeOutlineThickness":1,"brushHardness":"binary","activeLayerId":"fg","selectionIndices":[647],"rightClickUsesSecondary":true,"freeMoveMarkers":false,"trueFreeMoveMarkers":false,"uncappedScaling":false,"stationaryMarkers":false,"singleSelectionMoveSnapToGrid":false,"advancedMode":false,"renderObjectsBehindTiles":true,"eyedropUsesAllLayers":false,"eyedropCopiesMarkerProperties":true,"fillUsesDiagonals":false},"renderObjectsBehindTiles":true,"offsets":[[713,{"x":0.5,"y":0.5,"rotation":0,"scale":1.2,"flipH":false,"flipV":false}],[647,{"x":-0.5,"y":0,"rotation":322.5,"scale":1.2,"flipH":false,"flipV":false}],[764,{"x":0,"y":0,"rotation":90,"scale":1,"flipH":false,"flipV":false}]],"precisePlacements":[{"gridX":29,"gridY":23,"offsetX":0.5,"offsetY":0.5,"rotation":0,"scale":1.2,"flipX":false,"flipY":false},{"gridX":20,"gridY":24,"offsetX":-0.5,"offsetY":0,"rotation":322.5,"scale":1.2,"flipX":false,"flipY":fal